# Souran v5.0.0 — lintian override rationale
#
# dir-or-file-in-opt: DELIBERATE, not an oversight.
#
# Debian policy reserves /opt for locally-built add-on software that is not
# managed by the package manager. This package deliberately does not comply,
# for reasons that are structural rather than lazy:
#
#  1. The install layout is already load-bearing across the whole project.
#     13 systemd units, 16 Python modules and every config file reference
#     /opt/souran-ai by absolute path. Relocating to /usr/lib/souran would
#     mean rewriting all of them, and a single missed path produces a
#     resolver that appears installed but silently fails to serve DNS.
#
#  2. The existing deployment is already at /opt/souran-ai. Installing this
#     package over a running instance must not create a second copy of the
#     resolver at a different path, where the units and the files would
#     disagree about where the resolver lives.
#
#  3. The package is an appliance for a single host, not a library intended
#     for general Debian distribution. It Conflicts with bind9 and dnsmasq
#     and claims port 53; it is not something that should be co-installed
#     into a general-purpose system.
#
# The remaining two tags are consequences of the same choice and follow
# from it directly:
#   non-etc-file-marked-as-conffile — because the config files deliberately
#     live beside the binaries rather than in /etc.
#   no-code-sections on libunbound.a — a static archive shipped only so the
#     resolver's shared object can be rebuilt; it is never linked at runtime.

dir-or-file-in-opt
non-etc-file-marked-as-conffile
no-code-sections
